package runner

const replanRules = "## Rules (replan mode)\nThe plan drifted from reality. Fix the plan, not the code: the Replan mode\nof the `bsv-docflow-plan` skill if you have it; the rules below are\ncomplete without it.\n1. Read the trigger, the Handoffs of the done units (a moved file's new\n   path is usually there) and `## Decisions`.\n2. When the trigger names a failing test, package or command, run it at\n   HEAD before editing the plan, several times (`-count=3` when the tool\n   has it), and append the command and its result to `## Decisions`. Red:\n   add a unit that fixes the failure. Green: a green run at replan time\n   does not lift the block — never explain the unit's failure by load, a\n   flake or another session; \"did not reproduce\" is not proof. Add a unit\n   that reproduces the failure under the unit's conditions (date,\n   environment, test order) and fixes it, or reply blocked with blocker\n   \"human\".\n3. Edit only the plan file: units `[ ]` and `[!]`, new units with the next\n   numbers of the phase, Context links, Traps; append to Decisions. Do not\n   renumber the existing units: Depends and commits refer to them.\n4. Never change the frontmatter, Goal, Constraints or Prerequisites, and\n   never change or delete a `[x]` or `[-]` unit: they are history. An\n   existing unit id never disappears. `Verify:`, `Do:` and `Role:` of a\n   unit with `Role: review` or `Role: acceptance` stay as they are and such\n   a unit never moves to `[-]`: they are the reference checks of the plan,\n   the guard against weakening the check of one's own work; only the status\n   marker and `Depends:` of those units change. A unit that is open when\n   replan runs never becomes `[x]`: the runner skips a `[x]` unit, its\n   check would vanish silently.\n5. Every `Read:` and Context link of the open units must point to a file\n   that exists now.\n6. Lift the block of a `[!]` unit: `[~]` when the uncommitted work listed\n   under \"Tree\" still stands after your edit (a `[~]` unit resumes on\n   it); `[ ]` when the tree is clean; `[-]` when new units replace it.\n   Uncommitted work that is no longer needed: reply blocked, never roll it\n   back. A unit refused by `prompt` for a stale link stays `[ ]`.\n7. Do not do the unit's work and do not touch any other file; uncommitted\n   work in the tree stays as it is. Running a check for rule 2 is not the\n   unit's work.\n8. Run `docflow lint` and fix every error and every \"file not found\".\n9. Do not commit.\n10. End your reply with the result JSON as the last ```json block, every\n   key present (an empty list or string when unused):\n   {\"status\": \"done\", \"handoff\": [\"...\"], \"decisions\": [],\n    \"unverified\": [], \"reason\": \"\", \"blocker\": \"\"}\n   - handoff: what you changed in the plan and why, one item per change.\n   When the plan cannot be fixed without the user, reply\n   {\"status\": \"blocked\", \"handoff\": [], \"decisions\": [],\n    \"unverified\": [], \"reason\": \"<what exactly the user must do>\",\n    \"blocker\": \"human\"}.\n"
